{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    rounds = int(data[0].strip())\n    first_line = list(map(int, data[1].strip().split()))\n    second_line = list(map(int, data[2].strip().split()))\n\n    r1, s1, p1 = first_line\n    r2, s2, p2 = second_line\n\n    def solve_game():\n        # Calculate maximum wins\n        max_wins = 0\n        \n        # Rock(0) beats scissors(p2), Paper(1) beats rock(r2), Scissors(2) beats paper(s2)\n        # But indexing: first is rock, second is scissors, third is paper in second list?\n        # Let's map: first person: [rock, scissors, paper], second person: [rock, scissors, paper]\n        # First person wins: rock beats scissors, scissors beats paper, paper beats rock\n        # So use: rock(0) vs scissors(1), scissors(1) vs paper(2), paper(2) vs rock(0)\n        max_wins += min(r1, s2)\n        tmp_r1 = r1 - min(r1, s2)\n        tmp_s2 = s2 - min(r1, s2)\n        \n        max_wins += min(s1, p2)\n        tmp_s1 = s1 - min(s1, p2)\n        tmp_p2 = p2 - min(s1, p2)\n        \n        max_wins += min(p1, r2)\n        tmp_p1 = p1 - min(p1, r2)\n        tmp_r2 = r2 - min(p1, r2)\n\n        # For minimum wins, first eliminate same-type matches (draws)\n        same_rock = min(r1, r2)\n        r1 -= same_rock\n        r2 -= same_rock\n        \n        same_scissors = min(s1, s2)\n        s1 -= same_scissors\n        s2 -= same_scissors\n        \n        same_paper = min(p1, p2)\n        p1 -= same_paper\n        p2 -= same_paper\n\n        # Now count remaining wins possible in worst case\n        min_wins = 0\n        \n        # Try to use leftovers to create wins\n        if r1 > 0 and s2 > 0:\n            use = min(r1, s2)\n            min_wins += use\n            r1 -= use\n            s2 -= use\n            \n        if s1 > 0 and p2 > 0:\n            use = min(s1, p2)\n            min_wins += use\n            s1 -= use\n            p2 -= use\n            \n        if p1 > 0 and r2 > 0:\n            use = min(p1, r2)\n            min_wins += use\n            p1 -= use\n            r2 -= use\n\n        return min_wins, max_wins\n\n    min_val, max_val = solve_game()\n    print(f\"{min_val} {max_val}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        int rounds = Integer.parseInt(scanner.nextLine().trim());\n        String[] firstLine = scanner.nextLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        String[] secondLine = scanner.nextLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        \n        int r1 = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[0]);\n        int s1 = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[1]);\n        int p1 = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[2]);\n        \n        int r2 = Integer.parseInt(secondLine[0]);\n        int s2 = Integer.parseInt(secondLine[1]);\n        int p2 = Integer.parseInt(secondLine[2]);\n        \n        int[] result = solveGame(r1, s1, p1, r2, s2, p2);\n        System.out.println(result[0] + \" \" + result[1]);\n    }\n    \n    private static int[] solveGame(int r1, int s1, int p1, int r2, int s2, int p2) {\n        // Calculate maximum wins\n        int maxWins = 0;\n        \n        // Rock(0) beats scissors(p2), Paper(1) beats rock(r2), Scissors(2) beats paper(s2)\n        int win1 = Math.min(r1, s2);\n        maxWins += win1;\n        int tmpR1 = r1 - win1;\n        int tmpS2 = s2 - win1;\n        \n        int win2 = Math.min(s1, p2);\n        maxWins += win2;\n        int tmpS1 = s1 - win2;\n        int tmpP2 = p2 - win2;\n        \n        int win3 = Math.min(p1, r2);\n        maxWins += win3;\n        int tmpP1 = p1 - win3;\n        int tmpR2 = r2 - win3;\n        \n        // For minimum wins, first eliminate same-type matches (draws)\n        int sameRock = Math.min(r1, r2);\n        r1 -= sameRock;\n        r2 -= sameRock;\n        \n        int sameScissors = Math.min(s1, s2);\n        s1 -= sameScissors;\n        s2 -= sameScissors;\n        \n        int samePaper = Math.min(p1, p2);\n        p1 -= samePaper;\n        p2 -= samePaper;\n        \n        // Now count remaining wins possible in worst case\n        int minWins = 0;\n        \n        // Try to use leftovers to create wins\n        if (r1 > 0 && s2 > 0) {\n            int use = Math.min(r1, s2);\n            minWins += use;\n            r1 -= use;\n            s2 -= use;\n        }\n        \n        if (s1 > 0 && p2 > 0) {\n            int use = Math.min(s1, p2);\n            minWins += use;\n            s1 -= use;\n            p2 -= use;\n        }\n        \n        if (p1 > 0 && r2 > 0) {\n            int use = Math.min(p1, r2);\n            minWins += use;\n            p1 -= use;\n            r2 -= use;\n        }\n        \n        return new int[]{minWins, maxWins};\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001031